\title[Quantum groups as deformations of classical groups]
{Quantum Groups as Deformations of Classical Groups:\\
from $\Uq$ to Braided Categories and the Jones Polynomial}

\author{Aristotle}
\date{17 August 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We develop, with complete proofs, the bridge running from the $q$-deformed universal enveloping
algebra $\Uq$, through braided tensor structure, to a computable link invariant. We prove the
fundamental quadratic identity for symmetric quantum integers, exhibit each $\qint{m}$ in
denominator-free form, construct the $(n+1)$-dimensional highest-weight modules of $\Uq$
explicitly, and show that as $q\to1$ the deformed generators converge to the classical
$\mathfrak{sl}_2$ operators --- including the $0/0$ Cartan quotient
$(K-K^{-1})/(q-q^{-1})\to h$ --- with the limiting operators satisfying the undeformed relations.
We prove centrality of the quantum Casimir, compute its spectrum on the $(n+1)$-dimensional
module, and prove that its suitably shifted eigenvalue converges to $n(n+2)/4$. We prove the
higher commutator formula for $EF^m-F^mE$ and deduce the existence of singular vectors, and we
develop Gaussian binomials, both $q$-Pascal recursions, reflection symmetry, the $q$-binomial
theorem and its degeneration. On the topological side we prove invariance of the deformed
singlet, construct explicit Temperley--Lieb generators, prove that the Kauffman braiding is
invertible and satisfies the Yang--Baxter equation, prove that it intertwines the quantum-group
action, and derive a closed form for the bracket of every $(2,n)$ torus link; specialisations
give value $1$ for the unknot, $-A^4-A^{-4}$ for the Hopf link and $V=t+t^3-t^4$ for the
trefoil, whence the trefoil is distinguished from the unknot. Finally we prove that a binary
operation satisfies the set-theoretic Yang--Baxter equation if and only if it is
self-distributive, instantiate this at group conjugation, and prove modularity for abelian
anyons: nondegeneracy of a bicharacter implies $SS'=|A|\cdot\id$.
\end{abstract}

